Cost Analysis Summary
---------------------
🎯 Executive Summary & Purpose
-----------------------------------
The Cost Analysis Summary report provides a granular view of the company’s internal cost structure and transactional mechanics. 
It tracks procurement costs, vendor volume discounts, net financial obligations, and product return metrics. 
This enables operational leaders and finance teams to audit unit economics, optimize vendor negotiations, and effectively control expenditures.

📊 Visual Breakdown & Analytical Logic
---------------------------------------
Top-Level Cost Summary (KPI Cards):

1. Displays headline macro metrics to assess financial scale and vendor liabilities at a glance:

2. Cost / Unit: Tracks average product-level procurement expense.
 
3. Total Returns: Monitors total monetary value refunded, serving as an indicator of product quality or fulfillment issues.

4. Excess Units Sold: Quantifies sales volume exceeding baseline vendor agreement targets.

5. Net Payable to Vendors: Reflects the final liability owed to suppliers after applying volume-based tiered discounts.

Detailed Cost & Discount Breakdown (Matrix Visual):
----------------------------------------------------
1. Provides an itemized hierarchy analyzed by Product (SKU/Name), Month, and Vendor Agreement Code.
2. Allows leaders to audit month-over-month vendor performance, verify applied discount rates, and evaluate how sales volume directly offsets procurement costs.

Dynamic Threshold Slicer & Interactive Filters:
-------------------------------------------------
1. Threshold Parameter Slicer: Allows stakeholders to dynamically simulate and adjust vendor volume targets to analyze how changing discount thresholds impact total net margins and vendor payouts.

2. Global Slicers (Channel, Sub-Channel, Start of Month): Enables focused drill-downs into specific sales channels or date ranges to evaluate segment-specific cost efficiency.

💡 Key Takeaway
By combining dynamic vendor threshold modeling with itemized procurement breakdowns, 
this page transforms raw expense monitoring into an actionable cost-management tool—helping decision-makers protect net margins and negotiate stronger vendor terms.

